{
  "id": "main-effect",
  "term": "main effect",
  "definition": "A main effect is the effect of one independent variable considered across, or averaged over, all levels of the other variable or variables in a study. For example, it can describe the overall difference linked to one factor while ignoring how that difference may vary across another factor.",
